<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
         http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.3.xsd">

    <!--
      An unconfirmed reservation used to store its bookingId in hearing_id and leave booking_id
      null. That let the booking pipeline's hearing-wide release cover a re-pick for free, but it
      put a non-hearing value in a column named hearing_id, left booking_id null on the very rows
      that ARE a booking, and made "WHERE booking_id = ?" silently miss every live hold.

      No data migration ships with this: the feature is not live, so no production row was ever
      written in the old shape. Any row a test environment created before this change keeps its
      bookingId in hearing_id and is simply never matched again - harmless, and swept within a day
      by the nightly purge, which selects on expires_at alone and so finds them regardless.

      Reservations now use booking_id and leave hearing_id null until a share confirms them. A
      confirmed listing keeps both: the real hearing_id, and the booking_id it grew from. So
      expires_at - not which column is populated - is what tells the two apart:

        unconfirmed : booking_id = <bookingId>, hearing_id IS NULL,     expires_at IS NOT NULL
        confirmed   : booking_id = <bookingId>, hearing_id = <hearing>, expires_at IS NULL
    -->
    <!--
      court_schedule_hearing_id_idx (changeset 031) is UNIQUE on (court_schedule_id, hearing_id)
      and was what stopped one booking taking the same session twice. Postgres treats NULLs as
      distinct in a unique index, so once reservations leave hearing_id null it stops constraining
      them entirely. This partial index restores that guarantee on the column they now use, and is
      scoped to unconfirmed rows so it cannot interfere with confirmed listings.
    -->
    <changeSet id="053-unique-reservation-per-session" author="arcadius.ahouansou"
               logicalFilePath="053-move-reservation-booking-id-out-of-hearing-id.xml">
        <sql>
            CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS allocated_listings_reservation_idx ON
            allocated_listings(court_schedule_id, booking_id) WHERE expires_at IS NOT NULL;
        </sql>

        <rollback>
            <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS allocated_listings_reservation_idx;</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
      Live holds are looked up by booking_id on every status check and every release, so the
      unconfirmed rows need their own index rather than riding the confirmed listings' one.
    -->
    <changeSet id="053-index-booking-id" author="arcadius.ahouansou"
               logicalFilePath="053-move-reservation-booking-id-out-of-hearing-id.xml">
        <sql>
            CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS allocated_listings_booking_id_idx ON
            allocated_listings(booking_id);
        </sql>

        <rollback>
            <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS allocated_listings_booking_id_idx;</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
